            <ArticleTitle>Review: DSM-IV and pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>171-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The American Psychiatric Association recently published the fourth edition of its Diagnostic and Statistical Manual of Mental Disorders (DSM-IV). Although earlier editions included pain-related diagnosis, inherent problems in their construction limited their applicability. This article discusses how DSM-IV deals with pain, with a specific focus on the new diagnostic category of Pain Disorder.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
